{
 "format": "cpn-document",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "PathologyLab",
 "declarations": "(* The pathology lab from the supervisor's whiteboard sketch (2026-11-23): a use case showing\n   timed nets, a worker pool, performance reports and a delay computed by an external Python\n   function. Time is in minutes. *)\n\ncolset INT = int;\ncolset BOOL = bool;\ncolset CASE0 = record id : INT * arrived : INT;\ncolset CASE = CASE0 timed;\ncolset WORKER0 = product INT * INT;          (* worker id, skill *)\ncolset WORKER = WORKER0 timed;\ncolset JOB = product CASE0 * WORKER0 timed;  (* a case and the worker handling it *)\ncolset REVIEW = product CASE0 * BOOL timed;  (* a case after microscopy: more slides needed? *)\ncolset COUNTER = INT timed;\n\nvar c : CASE0;\nvar w, skill, n : INT;\nvar more : BOOL;\n\nval MEAN_GAP = 30.0;   (* minutes between arriving cases, on average *)\n\n(* A standard ML function, as CPN Tools has them. *)\nfun arrivalGap () = Int.max (1, round (exponential (1.0 / MEAN_GAP)));\nfun orderMore () = discrete (1, 10) = 1;   (* one case in ten needs more slides *)\n\n(* Computed by an external tool, Python (see patholab.py). CPN Tools uses this body instead. *)\n(* @python patholab.py delay_section *)\nfun delaySection (w : INT, skill : INT) : INT = 300 div skill;\n",
